# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Linux sanitizer job
# (.github/workflows/sanitize.yml, cmake/sanitize.cmake).
#
# Every line here names a LIBRARY WE DO NOT BUILD, and hides a leak only when
# that library is on the allocation's stack. They are the display, audio and
# GL stacks, which allocate for the life of the process and are not torn down
# at exit by design (Mesa's software renderer, ALSA's configuration tree, the
# X and Wayland client libraries). No entry names anything in this repository,
# the vendored libraries or the standard library: a leak in our own code must
# fail the job.
#
# These were written WITHOUT a Linux run to check them against (the job has not
# yet been run); prune any line the first log shows is not needed.
leak:libGLX_mesa
leak:libEGL_mesa
leak:libgallium
leak:swrast_dri
leak:libLLVM
leak:libX11
leak:libxcb
leak:libwayland
leak:libfontconfig
leak:libasound
leak:libdbus
